  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> be the inverse of the function <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>′</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math>, then <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mi>d</mi> <mrow> <mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow> </mfrac> <mi>ϕ</mi><mfenced> <mi>x</mi> </mfenced></mrow> </math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
